- Story & Context: Elias stood in the center of the laboratory, watching the pressure gauge climb as he pushed the cactus current to its breaking point. His colleague, Maren, begged him to stop, terrified that the plant’s feedback loop would damage their fragile hardware. The resulting sound was a searing, high-frequency whine that permanently altered the band’s signature tone. "Tell me you didn't touch the wire."
