Track 3: The Cartographer’s Thirst
- Story & Context: Years after the gardens were condemned, local scavengers claimed the site had become a sentient map, pointing toward buried, forgotten territories that no longer exist on any survey. The legend says if you play the song in the ruins at dawn, the plants will shift to reveal the hidden perimeter. Maren returned to the site one final time, finding only a scorched patch of earth where the speakers once stood. "We aren't lost, we are just misplaced."
